    "title": "Mike Phillips promoted to Unity Christian head boys' basketball coach - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Tristan Thomas ,\n2 hours ago\nDECATUR, Ill. (WCIA) — Unity Christian boys basketball is promoting from within for its next head boys basketball coach following Felipe Phillips’s departure to Mt. Zion.\nHe’s been an assistant coach around the Decatur area at various schools for about two decades, and he’s now stepping into his first head coaching gig.\nHere’s how he describes his coaching style:\n“I’m energetic; I’m exciting, I’m demanding, but I’m also a player’s coach,” Phillips said. “I want the kids to enjoy playing for me, and I think the hardest part about getting kids to buy in is getting them to respect you and understand what you want and do it to the best of your ability.” “Once they do that with confidence, I think the rest takes care of itself, and then the X’s and O’s, they can just leave up to me.”\nThe Lions are coming off a strong 2025-26 season after making a sectional game for the first time in school history, finishing with a 31-4 record.\nHe also played college basketball for two years at Wabash Valley, where he earned NJCAA All-American honors, followed by two seasons at Wichita State.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WCIA.com.",
